{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Come, let us deal wisely with him.</b> To come upon him by indirection." "<b>And he will go up from the land.</b> On his own initiative, without our having driven them out by force for any stated reason, so as to make us a byword among our enemies. And this would come to pass 'lest he multiply, and it come to pass that the travails of war befall us' — for תקראנה means that the evils and troubles of some war would befall us, as in וַתִּכַל דָּוִד (II Samuel 13:39), the soul of David." "<b>And he will join himself to our enemies.</b> For since they are distinguished from us by circumcision, by language, and by Hebrew customs, such that the Egyptians could not eat bread with the Hebrews (Genesis 43:32), they are undoubtedly our enemies, and they will reveal their hatred in time of the troubles of war."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:24:00.004598945Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}